,"author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution kickoff after signed plan-review PASS at origin/main 95f97cbeb6. Advisory disposition: adopt a meaningful savings bar of at least 50% focused median reduction for every modified family and at least 20 seconds aggregate same-host focused-suite wall reduction; use existing test-only parameter/env scaling where a real retry/timeout boundary must fire and clock injection only for passive test waits; remain within the four recorded file-impact paths. The function-level targets will be pinned by the required baseline profile before edits. The compound-AC advisory is accepted as formatting-only because the listed assertions and gates are intentionally atomic completion evidence; each result will still be recorded independently. Fresh worktree: /Users/joeoakhart/ci-clock-window-optimization on branch ci-clock-window-optimization. Landing path: one Gerrit change to refs/for/main, submit only after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1786831498610115001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation evidence before review: CI-matched baseline focused runs were 56.82s, 55.72s, 56.22s (median 56.22s). Final runs were 29.24s, 29.93s, 29.31s (median 29.31s), saving 26.91s / 47.9% across the focused set and clearing the >=20s aggregate bar. Each modified family cleared 50%: lock windows now preserve the real holder, dual-window flock/mkdir, real production backoff, attempt/warning/body-replay assertions at 2.5x holder/pass scale; shutdown uses the same 60/40 shared-budget geometry and a real thread barrier; autodeploy injects persisted episode age and models down-old/healthy-replacement while dedicated health-gate tests retain unhealthy rollback. reviewbot ensure was intentionally not edited because its ~15s is real clone/fetch/reconvergence/ensure/write durability, not a clock window. Exact-defect mutations remained RED after shortening: retries disabled 2/2 failed; fresh drain plus no in-flight gate 2/2 failed; episode reset plus unknown-as-busy 2/2 failed. Final focused four-file suite: 142 passed in 51.42s. CI-shaped default: 13,582 passed, 17 skipped in 1089.09s; integration: 167 passed, 2 skipped in 114.11s; no phase exceeded 30s. make lint and make typecheck passed. Production files and defaults are unchanged. Discovered security follow-up broadish-permanent-condor after pytest demonstrated ambient fixture values can appear in failure output; it is linked and out of this change.","timestamp":1786835076907748001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed commit fbab3290ba8827db283bf6bb5a431e0580610491 as Gerrit 1824 (Change-Id I87f7c818be79ccc55abfc75b2887ea43a7401422). Valid local rebar review-code PASS: 0 blocking, 0 advisory, attested at fbab3290ba. Awaiting independent LLM-Review and Verified votes; submit will follow immediately when both are +1 and no comments remain unresolved.","timestamp":1786835537157853001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 pushed as commit 8bb1ede9b0 (Gerrit 1824) after remediating the valid ordinal-stub advisory. DOWN_UNTIL_DEPLOY now transitions only when the stubbed docker compose up starts the replacement, so an extra curl cannot consume the transition. Added a separate zero-test-deadline persistent-DOWN case that asserts no drain deferral, deploy attempt, and rollback; this preserves the old persistently-unhealthy scenario without restoring the passive readiness wait. Verification: unreachable cases 2/2, full review-drain 14/14, dedicated health-gate 4/4, make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS. Existing Change-Id, DCO, and ticket trailer preserved.","timestamp":1786836492020191001}],"created_at":1786827587190293001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"553065e3-5b13-457d-b9fa-5bcfdb4b5d4b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"815d-8f56-7237-4b58"},{"link_uuid":"154c4723-8f6c-40e4-921b-871ca8b2ffc6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"039b-d179-b669-4439"},{"link_uuid":"08caebb8-9abb-4e60-9e2b-04dc03a25819","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"124e-ecfa-74c9-4814"},{"link_uuid":"bca734a5-35d9-4d8c-9539-0320bac4a275","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6d6c-d295-f531-4f76"},{"link_uuid":"c4f2e6c1-1fea-483e-a9b6-66fa0c23390a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8d1d-8a0e-e05c-47de"},{"link_uuid":"d907abbd-cd16-4a82-8a58-4f6f7a918127","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cea5-5beb-7b2b-4411"},{"link_uuid":"783f0781-7bea-4069-9a94-d6369bf90ddc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9a75-a619-60f9-471f"}],"description":"## Context\nThe exhaustive current-main macOS census found remaining multi-second costs caused by test-scale wall-clock windows rather than useful production work: review-bot ticket bootstrap is about 10.15 worker-phase seconds per cell, lock-retry coverage totals about 15.56s per cell, review-bot shutdown cases are about 9s per cell, and autodeploy coverage includes an explicit 3s sleep plus an 8.25s unreachable-health case. Production timeout, retry, drain, and health budgets are contractual and must remain unchanged.\n\nClosed classless-dainty-lamprey already proved and landed the same pattern for snapshot low-speed and retry tests. Maintained OSS consensus supports the direction: CPython uses 0.05-0.1s trigger windows with generous cleanup deadlines, and urllib3 injects or scales backoff while retaining real sockets. Ticket history requires retaining real subprocess, lock, process-group, and health behavior: royal-weariless-zebrafish, odorful-epidemic-shelduck, balsamy-eloquent-iggypops, equestrian-clueless-cowbird, and unskillful-supportive-lion.\n\n## Plan\n- Reprofile each named family alone on current main and record wall and worker-phase baselines.\n- Freeze behavioral contract cards for attempt counts, logical backoff schedules, real lock/process/socket behavior, terminal states, cleanup, and exact error/observability output.\n- Inject or scale only test-owned clocks/windows; retain real boundary execution and generous teardown polling.\n- Prove each final oracle RED against an exact-defect mutation before implementation, then GREEN.\n- Run focused suites, lint, typecheck, and full Gerrit Verify; report per-cell and aggregate runner savings and the first post-merge organic observation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Production timeout, retry, drain, health, and backoff defaults are byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- [ ] Real subprocess, lock, process-group, and health boundary coverage remains enabled.\n- [ ] Each shortened case preserves attempt counts, logical schedule, terminal state, cleanup, and observability assertions.\n- [ ] Each case has legitimate RED-to-GREEN and exact-defect mutation evidence.\n- [ ] Same-host before/after timings report macOS wall and total runner savings.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and merge are recorded before closure.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_reviewbot_ensure_tickets.py","reason":"Scale only test-owned ticket-bootstrap trigger windows while retaining real Git behavior."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py","reason":"Scale test-owned lock/retry windows while preserving real acquisition and logical retry contracts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"Scale test-owned shutdown/review trigger windows while preserving production drain defaults."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py","reason":"Replace explicit wall sleeps with bounded deterministic test triggers while retaining script behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","039b-d179-b669-4439"],["relates_to","124e-ecfa-74c9-4814"],["relates_to","6d6c-d295-f531-4f76"]